From: Viktor Semykin <thesame.ml@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] loader: preserve auxiliary identity with either libdrm ABI

Normalize auxiliary nodes to an internal platform-shaped descriptor using
only the public stock libdrm ABI. Store the child identity independently
of its PCI parent, and use the same auxiliary DRI_PRIME tag whether libdrm
recognizes the node or the sysfs fallback supplies it. Recover driver PCI
IDs from the parent without representing the child as that PCI device.

This follows the existing Cedarview sysfs fallback. No private bus enum or
union layout is needed by Mesa. Test child identity, parent hardware IDs,
node grouping and tag lifetime after removal with the fake sysfs tree.

Signed-off-by: Viktor Semykin <thesame.ml@gmail.com>

